# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, Git on Windows checks shell scripts and SQL out with CRLF.
# A .sh file with CRLF fails inside a Linux container with the notoriously
# unhelpful "not found" error (the shell is looking for an interpreter whose
# name ends in \r), and psql chokes on CRLF in a heredoc. Forcing LF on
# everything the containers execute removes that entire class of failure.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh          text eol=lf
*.sql         text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf

# Windows-native tooling keeps CRLF so it opens cleanly in Notepad and runs
# under PowerShell without complaint.
*.ps1         text eol=crlf
*.bat         text eol=crlf
*.cmd         text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
.expo/
